I understand you're feeling overwhelmed in your marriage.  

While divorce is an option, many find this path deeply traumatic for both themselves and their adult children. Instead, consider these compassionate approaches:  

1) Set boundaries by temporarily living separately while maintaining your joint finances - most people can't divorce but still want space;  

2) Engage in couples therapy, as communication issues often resolve with proper guidance;  

3) If physical violence has occurred (even if only once), immediately seek restraining orders and document all incidents;  

4) If emotional manipulation or financial control feels like your only issue, you may need a financial separation rather than separation from him entirely.  

Consider how many marriages fail due to financial stress rather than personal incompatibility before taking irreversible legal action.
